{
  "_comment": "Maps each feed key to lines in a supplier quote CSV. `patterns`: case-insensitive regexes on the description column (any one matches); `exclude`: regexes that reject a line even if a pattern matched; `skus`: exact matches on the sku/part column (checked first, ignore exclude). `per` is the feed unit: `each` (default; UOM C = /100, M = /1000, and 'BAG OF 100' or '1000/BX' in the text divide by the pack), `ft` (UOM FT/LF used as is, else divided by the stick/bar/coil length in the text, else by `divideBy`), `roll50` (fabric per 50' roll; 100' rolls are halved, per-foot prices x50). `manual: true` keys are never priced from a quote. The first line that matches wins. Edit these to match how YOUR supplier words their lines; test with: node update-feed.js quote <file.csv> --dry-run",
  "settings.markup": {
    "manual": true,
    "_note": "your markup %, not a supplier price"
  },
  "settings.tax": {
    "manual": true,
    "_note": "sales tax %, not a supplier price"
  },
  "fabricRoll.4": {
